==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|háll}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*hēlaz|t=slippery, deceitful}}, related to {{cog|gml|hāl||hidden}} and {{cog|goh|hāli||smooth, slippery, weak}}. Further etymology unsure. Maybe from the Proto-Indo-European root {{m|ine-pro|*ḱel-||to hide}} (cf. Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*helaną|t=to conceal, hide}}), or from {{m|ine-pro|*ḱelH-||to freeze}}, or from {{m|ine-pro|*kel-||to incline}}. Possible cognates in Icelandic are {{m|is|héla||hoarfrost}} and {{m|is|hagl||hail}}.<ref>{{R:ine:NIL|page=416}}</ref><ref>{{R:gem:EDPG|head=Hēli-}}</ref>

